{"kind":"assert","text":"Approved. Use a scratch-only read adapter outside the checkout. It uses the checked-in client's bounded SQL and response rules and calls evaluateDeployment with a null bound. Keep its source in the evidence directory with its SHA-256 and the output hashes, so a reader can rerun it. Make only the Demo analytics reads and the public health reads.\n\nRecord one gap in the notes-only head: the deploy-check CLI cannot make its own first calibration, because it requires a prior bound. Do not fix that in this request. Name it in the Status line as an open item. The first bound then makes the CLI usable from the second deploy on, and a later head can add an explicit calibration mode if the next deploy shows a need.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}